  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: spring-security-saml2-service-provider 5.7.11.rhlw-00006",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.springframework.security:spring-security-saml2-service-provider 5.7.11.rhlw-00006 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-40988, CVE-2026-41003, and CVE-2026-41694.\n\nCVE-2026-40988: Unbounded DEFLATE Inflation in SAML 2.0 Service Provider\n\nCVE-2026-41003: Unencoded HTML Outputs in Spring Security May Allow Cross-Site Scripting\n\nCVE-2026-41694: SAML Payloads Decrypted Without Valid Signature\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.springframework.security:spring-security-saml2-service-provider 5.7.11 from Maven Central.",
